    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1530">

                <pb facs="0984" n="868" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg868"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/46.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul General Hanna to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monterey</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-27T08:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1914, 8 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s inquiry concerning French Brothers who were forced to leave Monterey
                    and who went to Havana via Brownsville, Texas, I understand that no money was
                    collected from them. I rendered them considerable friendly assistance. I will
                    inquire as to the matter of school property and as to their return and report
                    soon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
